-- §1  Every site the model does arithmetic at, and what guards the join.
# One row per site on arithmetic/roster.sqlc: how many instances may be worked out, how many are
# suspended by a typed blank, how many put two numbers of different kinds together, and the rule
# that checks the figures are the same kind of thing.
#
# The column to read is `guarded_by!`
#   Run it alone and look there. Most of the sites are blank. The remainder is one of them: the
#   central calculation in the model, a subtraction across two unit columns that nothing compares.
#
# A blank guard is not a pass
#   A blank guard beside a zero in `not_comparable!` is a site whose luck has not run out: the
#   corpus happens to agree everywhere today, which is exactly the state that reads as safe and is
#   not.
-- arithmetic/roster.sqlc beside folds/site_subjects.sqlc, one row per declared site.
SELECT r.site                        AS "site!",
       coalesce(r.guarded_by, '')    AS "guarded_by!",
       f.computable                  AS "computable!",
       f.suspended                   AS "suspended!",
       f.not_comparable              AS "not_comparable!"
FROM (
    :compose(arithmetic/roster.sqlc)
) r
JOIN (
    :compose(folds/site_subjects.sqlc)
) f ON f.subject = r.site
ORDER BY r.slug
